Package: kodemo
Version: @VERSION@
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Kodemo contributors <noreply@kodemo.dev>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.31), libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, libgl1, libx11-6, libxkbcommon0, libfontconfig1, libgomp1, zlib1g, libzstd1, libssl3t64 | libssl3
Recommends: libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0, curl, libgl1-mesa-dri
Suggests: git
Description: native Rust code editor for modest machines
 Kodemo is a small, native IDE written in Rust with egui. It offers a
 VS Code-style editor, a file tree, a built-in terminal, an optional local
 Qwen ghost-completion model, and a WebKit live preview.
 .
 It uses far less memory than Electron editors and ships dark, light and
 high-contrast themes designed for old laptops.
